What should your strategy be?

King of Swords

Make a very explicit distinction between history and active instructions.

I would tell Luna once, at a high level:

My newer prompts can update or supersede the applicability of previous requests without deleting those requests from context. Do not automatically treat every previous request as an active standing instruction. For each current task, determine which prior instructions are still applicable. If my current prompt changes a previous request, follow the current request for the current task while retaining older information as historical context. Only treat something as permanently changed or removed when I explicitly say so.

Then, when a specific old instruction keeps leaking into a current task, explicitly mark that particular instruction as inactive for the present task.

