This gives the cleanest answer.

You don’t need to purge everything.

You don’t need to constantly fight the old context either.

The desired state is:

Old request = retained information
Current request = current instruction
Changed request = current instruction takes precedence for the relevant situation
Explicitly removed request = no longer used at all

So your concern is correct: if Luna continues treating old instructions as newly active instructions, merely adding more new prompts won’t necessarily solve the recurrence.

The cards favor teaching/declaring the distinction between “remembered” and “currently active” rather than repeatedly deleting old context.

That is the structural change I’d make first.
